    "narrative": "For the Austin Waves on August 5, 2026, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** leads our daily efficiency board with a 72.16 score, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Pallante. While **Jacob Wilson** (66.56) also earns a high-confidence start batting second, our most efficient path to upside lies in the middle-infield stack. **Kyle Tucker** (63.20) and **Sam Antonacci** (61.55) anchor our outfield, with **Sam Antonacci** benefitting from a prime leadoff spot and favorable platoon dynamics against Gray. **Jackson Merrill** (61.00) remains a lock despite a platoon disadvantage against Bratt; his 6.59 xERA matchup is simply too inviting to bench, offering the highest ceiling for counting stats on the day.\n\nThe primary lineup crunch today centered on **Jorge Polanco**, who finished just off the cut at 53.21. While **Jorge Polanco** provided solid baseline metrics, the lower batting order position and the superior matchup quality for **Miguel Vargas** (53.22)\u2014who carries a strong 0.389 xwOBA\u2014pushed **Miguel Vargas** into the final starting spot. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor **Drake Baldwin**, whose 56.52 efficiency is accompanied by a 33% rain risk. With **Jordan Westburg** sidelined on the IL and both **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Luis Robert Jr.** absent from the daily rotation, our depth is being tested; however, the speed profiles of **Nasim Nunez** (60.12) and **Andy Pages** (57.54) ensure we remain competitive in the scarcest category, SB, even as we navigate the volatility of **Drake Baldwin**\u2019s weather-impacted start.",
